Creates a mock webserver for the webapp to mock handling requests until the backend api is ready. To keep things are **modular** as possible, `MockServer.js` imports the exported `handlers` array from all feature modules exported from `features` module to setup the server. 
Therefore all features have to export `handlers` and be exported from the `features` module to ensure their `msw.rest` handlers are included in the webserver. For more information on MSW, check out their [documentation](https://mswjs.io/docs/)
```.js
// features/MyFeature/index.js
export {handlers}

// features/index.js
export * as MyFeature from './MyFeature';
``` 
When set up, the MockServer will intercept all requests and respond with the handler's return value

*To run the test run `npm test`*
